            "messageBody": "\u2026caffolds\n\nThree problems in the app/ layout, all of them things a judge would trip over\nbefore we did.\n\n`audio_test` and `jpeg_test` were never in the firmware.  An app under `app/`\nis only seen by Kconfig once the manifest's <linkfile> has soft-linked it into\n`packages/demos/contest2026_264_<name>`, and those two links did not exist in\nthe work tree -- the other three were created by hand, which is why only they\nhappened to work.  With the link missing, `=y` in a defconfig is dropped in\nsilence: no warning, app absent, build \"successful\".  Restoring both links\ntakes nsh from 408384 to 485184 bytes of flash; that 75 KB was two missing\napps, not a saving.  README now spells the trap out next to the mapping table.\n\n`app/hello_app/` was the scaffold's name but not its content: it built\n`ctrlc_test` (from `hello_app_main.c`) and `periph_selftest`, defined neither\na HELLO_APP symbol nor a `hello_app` command, shipped a `Make.defs` still\npointing at the template's `contest2026_000_hello_app`, and had no Makefile\nentry for `periph_selftest` at all -- only the cmake path could build it.\n`ctrlc_test` moves to `app/ctrlc_test/` here with its own Kconfig, Makefile\nand Make.defs; `periph_selftest` follows in the next commit, because moving it\ntouches somebody else's file.\n\n`quickapp/hello_quickapp/` and `board/contest_board/` were empty\n`contest2026_000` samples, soft-linked into the build tree, in a repo whose\nreal board code is `board/beken/`.  Deleted, with their <linkfile> entries.\n\nAlso here, on files this commit already owns: the `ai_agent` README's Network\nsection claimed the AP has no network device (it has had a netdev STA driver\nsince d093016) and quoted a heap measured before the network stack landed;\nboth are replaced with current, sourced numbers, and the footprint table is\nre-measured with all six links in place.  `bk7258_ramdisk.c`'s rationale said\ntmpfs cannot hold a frame because the heap is ~300 KB, which stopped being\ntrue when the system heap reached into PSRAM.\n\nVerified on hardware, nsh config, all-app.bin repackaged with the three\nsha256 equal: `help` lists audio_test, camera_preview, ctrlc_test, hello,\njpeg_test and periph_selftest; `periph_selftest` reports SELFTEST PASS\nfailures=0; `ctrlc_test` receives its SIGINT; `jpeg_test` and `audio_test`\nboth run.",
